# PCI capability lists: what each device can do (drivers todo, item P3).
# The e1000e card has a list; the old chipset devices of the QEMU PC have none.
@wire
@e1000e
$ lspci -v
~ ^00:00\.0 8086:1237 Host bridge$
~ ^00:0\d\.0 8086:10d3 Ethernet controller \(IRQ \d+\)$
~ ^        power management, MSI, PCI Express, MSI-X$
# Without -v: the plain list, one line per device.
$ lspci
~ ^00:0\d\.0 8086:10d3 Ethernet controller \(IRQ \d+\)$
$ lspci -x
~ lspci: wrong arguments
